## The Golden Rule: Never Block the Main Thread

On mobile platforms, the **Main Thread (UI Thread)** is solely responsible for rendering frames at 60Hz (16.6ms per frame) or 120Hz ProMotion (8.3ms per frame) and responding to user gestures. 

If your code executes heavy loops, synchronous JSON parsing, or network calls on the main thread:
* **On Android:** Triggers an **ANR (Application Not Responding)** dialog after 5 seconds, prompting the user to force-close the app.
* **On iOS:** Triggers the system **Watchdog timer**, which abruptly terminates the application process (crash exception code `0x8badf00d`).

### Concurrency Code Patterns Across Stacks

<Tabs>
  <TabItem label="React Native (TypeScript)">

In React Native, JavaScript runs on its own engine thread, while native rendering occurs on the UI thread. Long-running synchronous calculations freeze touch responses; use `useTransition` or worker pools:

```typescript
import React, { useState, useTransition } from 'react';
import { View, Text, FlatList, TextInput, ActivityIndicator, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

export function SearchableDirectory({ dataset }: { dataset: Array<{ id: string; name: string }> }) {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('');
  const [filteredData, setFilteredData] = useState(dataset);
  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition();

  const handleSearch = (text: string) => {
    setQuery(text);

    // Non-blocking transition: preserves instant typing responsiveness on UI thread
    startTransition(() => {
      const lower = text.toLowerCase();
      const results = dataset.filter(item => item.name.toLowerCase().includes(lower));
      setFilteredData(results);
    });
  };

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <TextInput
        value={query}
        onChangeText={handleSearch}
        placeholder="Search directory..."
        placeholderTextColor="#9ca3af"
        style={styles.input}
      />
      {isPending && <ActivityIndicator color="#22c55e" style={styles.loader} />}
      <FlatList
        data={filteredData}
        keyExtractor={item => item.id}
        renderItem={({ item }) => <Text style={styles.itemText}>{item.name}</Text>}
      />
    </View>
  );
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
